        "id": 7021,
        "name": "Heckbringer",
        "username": "Heckbringer",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/58956e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-11T14:33:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello, everyone! I'm new to this game and I'm loving it, as are all the people I'm introducing it to!</p><p>One of the things that draws me to certain games is being able to imagine what happened during a turn, and this game is tightly themed enough that I find it to be very satisfying in that regard, but I have run into one card combination that stands out as something that I'm having trouble explaining, and I was wondering what happens in other peoples' heads to justify it... Why do discarded bursts help Tachyon do damage, and what's happening when they get discarded?</p><p>Ideas I've got so far:</p><p>1) Extra \"burst\" of acceleration that adds to her current velocity, which I like, but it might only make sense if she doesn't change direction, which I feel like she'd kind of have to in order to accomplish all that she does (or maybe not?).</p><p>2) She's warming up either physically or mentally.</p><p>3) She's dosing herself with a \"burst\" of stimulant.</p><p>4) She's getting hit with a \"burst\" of blood-lust.</p><p>Any thoughts appreciated.</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:10.875Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
