        "raw": "<p>Hello, everyone! I&#39;m new to this game and I&#39;m loving it, as are all the people I&#39;m introducing it to!</p><p>One of the things that draws me to certain games is being able to imagine what happened during a turn, and this game is tightly themed enough that I find it to be very satisfying in that regard, but I have run into one card combination that stands out as something that I&#39;m having trouble explaining, and I was wondering what happens in other peoples&#39; heads to justify it... Why do discarded bursts help Tachyon do damage, and what&#39;s happening when they get discarded?</p><p>Ideas I&#39;ve got so far:</p><p>1) Extra &quot;burst&quot; of acceleration that adds to her current velocity, which I like, but it might only make sense if she doesn&#39;t change direction, which I feel like she&#39;d kind of have to in order to accomplish all that she does (or maybe not?).</p><p>2) She&#39;s warming up either physically or mentally.</p><p>3) She&#39;s dosing herself with a &quot;burst&quot; of stimulant.</p><p>4) She&#39;s getting hit with a &quot;burst&quot; of blood-lust.</p><p>Any thoughts appreciated.</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
