      {
        "id": 51905,
        "name": "Alex",
        "username": "Alex",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/alex/{size}/2059_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-11T22:33:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, I'd say the bursts are bursts of speed.</p><p>On a similar note, I've been thinking of Absolute Zero's mechanics and it got me wondering...</p><p>how much of what he does with the suit was an intended feature when it was built? I mean, obviously it was built for some combat since they wanted Frost to be a superhero, but do you think he's supposed to weild it as recklessly as he does? It's easy to see why he'd be pretty resentful about how they made him join, and his tragic past can't be helping his attitude either. I get the impression Ryan Frost is often sort of \"exploiting\" the devices to just get this over with faster, heedless of whatever damage he's causing to them. If nothing else, it's pretty funny to imagine it like this.</p><p>Tachyon: \"What are you doing!? That was just for regulating your temperature! You aren't supposed to DELIBERATELY overheat it!\"</p><p>Absolute Zero: \"SEE IF I CARE!\"</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:25:39.638Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
