        "raw": "<p>Yeah, I&#39;d say the bursts are bursts of speed.</p><p>On a similar note, I&#39;ve been thinking of Absolute Zero&#39;s mechanics and it got me wondering...</p><p>how much of what he does with the suit was an intended feature when it was built? I mean, obviously it was built for some combat since they wanted Frost to be a superhero, but do you think he&#39;s supposed to weild it as recklessly as he does? It&#39;s easy to see why he&#39;d be pretty resentful about how they made him join, and his tragic past can&#39;t be helping his attitude either. I get the impression Ryan Frost is often sort of &quot;exploiting&quot; the devices to just get this over with faster, heedless of whatever damage he&#39;s causing to them. If nothing else, it&#39;s pretty funny to imagine it like this.</p><p>Tachyon: &quot;What are you doing!? That was just for regulating your temperature! You aren&#39;t supposed to DELIBERATELY overheat it!&quot;</p><p>Absolute Zero: &quot;SEE IF I CARE!&quot;</p>",
